window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>I don’t do romance. I don’t do love. I certainly don’t do relationships. Women are attracted to my power and money and I like a nice ass and a pretty smile. It’s a fair exchange—a business deal for pleasure.</p> <p>Meeting Beth Harrison in the first class cabin of my flight from Chicago to London throws me for a loop and everything I know about myself and women goes out the window.</p> <p>I’m usually good at reading people, situations, the markets. I know instantly if I can trust someone or if they’re lying. But Beth is contradictory and confounding I don’t know which way is up.</p> <p>She’s sweet but so much more, she makes my knees weak and mouth dry. She’s confident but so vulnerable, I want to wrap her up and protect her from the world.</p> <p>We spend the night together and then just disappears, leaving me with my pants around my ankles, wondering which day of the week it is. If I ever see her again I don’t know if I’ll scream at her, strip her naked or fall in love.</p> <p>Thank goodness I live in Chicago and she lives in London and we’ll never see each other again, right?</p> <p>A stand-alone, full length novel with no cliffhanger.</p>"; 
